          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is there a pumpkin spice protein powder without artificial sweeteners?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Naked Shake Pumpkin Spice uses cane sugar, Truvani Pumpkin Spice uses monk fruit, and Orgain uses erythritol and stevia, per their labels at the time of writing. The whey picks on this list use sucralose and acesulfame potassium. For full control, make a DIY shake from an unsweetened vanilla, purée, spice and a little maple syrup."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pumpkin spice protein powder the same as pumpkin seed protein?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Pumpkin spice protein powder is a flavor, usually whey or pea protein flavored with cinnamon and other spices. Pumpkin seed protein is a plant protein made from pressed pumpkin seeds, typically sold unflavored with a green tint and nutty taste. Our separate pumpkin seed protein powder guide covers that product for people who want a pea-free plant protein."
